omx-clap-host (0.35.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * release: the RPM is x86_64 only, as the build requirements it is built
    against are
  * The contract directory has no schema-major level: omx-clap's package sits
    beside its domain
  * domains: every domain is at 0.1.0, its vocabulary own version, never the
    package one
  * The wave's merges, repaired: catalog-gate, #219's sources, the jalv test
    in CI
  * 0.M.m until 1.0: every domain stays at the package version, as the wave
    had them
  * No version bump while developing: VERSION, the spec and the omx-clap
    domain stay where the wave has them
  * 0.36.0: the spec's version and the changelog line; the hosting codes
    module rendered again
  * omx-clap-contract leaves the domain host to
    plugin-hostd-protocol-contract (ruling R5)
  * changelogs: the entries in date order
  * deps.txt: the omx-contract and libomx-domain rows are 3.22.0, rendered
  * .gitignore: tests/clap_properties_test is a build output
  * domains never go back: revert 0.35.0's renumber to the package version
  * ci.yml: run the shared trigger gate
  * release: a merge to devel publishes the real package to staging
  * ci: a pull request into devel accepts staged omx packages; every other
    run still refuses them (#224)
  * V23d: dbPerOct and dbPerS map onto the standard ids dBPerOct and dBPerS
  * V23d: arm (r) refuses a second sheet of strings anywhere in the omx-clap
    package, and ids rows in the units header
  * V23d: the ids header is a package-scope entry of the domain's root
    x-render; no item carries a render
  * V23d: red first, every render of the domain is its root x-render, and the
    ids header is a package-scope root entry
  * V23d: arm (c) reads PARAM_UNITS_CLAP_ENCODED as the words item it is
    ruled to be, and refuses any other kind by name
  * V23d: arm (c) reads PARAM_UNITS_CLAP_ENCODED by name, whatever its kind
  * V23d: red first, arm (c) holds the mapping onto omx-contract's
    PARAM_UNITS_CLAP_ENCODED, exactly
  * V23d: the both-headers test leaves: in chain 3 omx-contract's unit header
    no longer exists
  * V23d: the both-headers sabotage goes red only on the moved row, the
    quoted include is refused, and the ids have a swap arm
  * V23d: red first, the no-copy check also refuses the quoted include of
    omx-contract's old unit header
  * V23d: the CHANGELOG says what moved
  * V23d: omx-clap renders both headers, and the code -> standard id lookup
    is omx_param_unit_ids.h
  * V23d: red first, the renders are omx-clap's and the code -> standard id
    lookup is a rendered header
  * V23d: the tokens map onto the standard ids, the PARAM_UNITS consts (dB,
    Hz, deg, dB-oct)
  * V23d: red first, each token maps to its standard id, the PARAM_UNITS
    const as released
  * V23d: src/omx_param_units.h has its own guard, OMX_CLAP_PARAM_UNITS_H
  * V23d: red first, this tree's unit header and omx-contract's old copy
    compile in one unit under -Werror
  * V23d: the param-contract code sheet is this tree's, and omx_clap_ext.h
    reads its own render
  * V23d: red first, the unit code sheet is this tree's domain
    omx-param-contract, mapped to the standard units
  * code-text-check: a words item's words are ours, keyed ITEM.word
  * C2 findings on #221: the fuzz corpus copy of verb-hosts, the scan check
    reads the package as installed
  * C2 findings on #221: the installer gets the package, the renders carry
    HOSTING_VERB_HOSTS
  * omx-clap 0.34.2: the served omx-contract 3.22.0 reads the installed
    package
  * host-replies-check holds every table-typed reply this source writes, read
    from its registrations, not only those with a HOST_FIELDS macro
  * note_input, note_drops and note_out_drops are typed by
    plugin-hostd-protocol's table: drop them from OMX_CLAP_REPLIES
  * The host words, the verb hosts and the shared verbs are
    plugin-hostd-protocol's: read them from there (ruling R5)
  * ci.yml: a pull request into devel may take its packages from the staging
    channel
  * .githooks/commit-msg is the shared stub, byte for byte
  * no_floors_check: rpm's epoch prefix %{?epoch:%{epoch}:} is generated,
